                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma_0
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\left(
                  \\begin{array}{cc}
                  1 &amp; 0
                  \\\
                  0 &amp; 1
                  \\end{array}
                  \\right)
                  ,\;\;\;\;
                  \\sigma_1
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\left(
                  \\begin{array}{cc}
                  0 &amp; 1
                  \\\
                  1 &amp; 0
                  \\end{array}
                  \\right)
                  ,\;\;\;\;
                  \\sigma_2
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\left(
                  \\begin{array}{cc}
                  0 &amp; -\mathrm{i}
                  \\\
                  \\mathrm{i} &amp; 0
                  \\end{array}
                  \\right)
                  ,\;\;\;\;
                  \\sigma_3
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\left(
                  \\begin{array}{cc}
                  1 &amp; 0
                  \\\
                  0 &amp; -1
                  \\end{array}
                  \\right)
                  \\,.
          %p#TraditionalCircuit
            In this case, the component-evaluation of the above diagram yields the quantum teleportation protocol in its traditional form (due to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BBCJPW93"} BBCJPW93
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+circuit"} quantum circuit
            (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Quipper#GLRSV13"} GLRSV13, p. 5
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbits"} qbits
            (where “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            ” denotes the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+gate"} Hadamard gate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+CNOT+gates"} quantum CNOT gates
            and the boxed pointers denote
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+measurement"} quantum measurement
            in the
            = succeed "-basis):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbit"} qbit
          %center
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/QBitQuantumTeleportationProtocol-221109.jpg", :width => "800"}/
          %p
            %br/
          %p The concrete implementation of the above protocol on given quantum hardware will look more complicated.
          %p#AsABraidGateCircuit
            For instance, the implementation of the quantum teleportation protocol as a circuit of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+representation"} braid
            gates of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ising+anyons"} Ising anyons
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+computation"}> topological quantum computation
            ) is given in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#XuZhou22"} Xu &amp; Zhou 2022
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BraidCircuitQuantumTeleProtocol-220915.jpg", :width => "450"}/
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Valera23"} Valera (2023)
          %p
